    "created_at": "2021-11-21T10:39:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-21T10:41:45Z",
    "body": "Thank you for the concrete example for where conditionals could come in handy.\r\nBalancing between keeping configuration simple and allowing for powerful configuration has been on my mind lately. I think that, instead of extending the Starship DSL, it may be best if we add support for proper scripting for more advanced configuration using logical operators.\r\n\r\nIf we add if/else, we'll eventually need logical and/or/not operators, then we'll need to add comments to explain complex logic, and so on. We'd be gradually rebuilding a simple language.\r\n\r\nI think #2502 is headed in the right direction in this regard. 😄 \r\nPerhaps not having a scripting language to replace `starship.toml`, but per-module opt-in scripting could be the solution.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
